      "updated": 1783362088444,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Our analysts spend 4-6 hours per company researching SEC filings, \nearnings calls, and news. Design a GenAI system that reduces this to 30 minutes.\"",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"Our analysts spend 4-6 hours per company researching SEC filings, \nearnings calls, and news. Design a GenAI system that reduces this to 30 minutes.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ivuLM4Qi2jnNxwaC4CW3d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 162.03750610351562,
      "y": 325.98907470703125,
      "width": 822.9793701171875,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2041357409,
      "version": 33,
      "versionNonce": 1279582561,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783362363056,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Users: 50-200 analysts\n- Data: SEC filings (10-K, 10-Q, 8-K), earnings call transcripts, news, analyst reports\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Users: 50-200 analysts\n- Data: SEC filings (10-K, 10-Q, 8-K), earnings call transcripts, news, analyst reports\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_GwhthoUwgr0a8I5SriOb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 262.19999702453606,
      "y": 543.6406240653992,
      "width": 747.0994262695312,
      "height": 1250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 329876143,
      "version": 736,
      "versionNonce": 1302573409,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783362514392,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR:\n1. Freeform Q&A: \"whats current risk, scope, outlook for AAPL\"\n    -> structured, annotated, grounded answer with citations\n2. Company profile subscriptions: user defines watchlist + format\n    -> agent processes async, delivers on schedule (daily/weekly)\n3. Comparative analysis: \"Compare NVDA vs AMD risk factors\" or\n    \"How did AAPL guidance change vs last quarter?\"\n    -> semantic diff across documents, not just retrieval\n4. Multi-hop reasoning: \"Which of my covered companies have supply\n    chain exposure to Taiwan AND revenue >$50B?\"\n    -> decompose into sub-queries (structured filter + semantic + join)\n5. Numerical queries: \"What was NVDA gross margin trend over 4 quarters?\"\n    -> must use structured data/SQL, NOT hallucinate numbers from RAG\n6. Contradiction handling: news says 'beat', analyst says 'miss'\n    -> detect conflicts, present both with source authority ranking\n7. Follow-up / conversational: \"Drill into the top risk\" after prior answer\n    -> maintain context, resolve anaphora (\"the\", \"it\", \"that\")\n8. Chart/table extraction: \"Show me the revenue breakdown table from 10-K pg 47\"\n    -> multi-modal: parse tables, describe charts, extract structured data\n9. Cross-reference resolution: answer mentions 'See Note 12'\n    -> auto-fetch Note 12 content and include in response\n10. Proactive alerts: new 8-K filed for watched company\n    -> detect, summarize, push notification to relevant analyst\n11. Report generation: \"Generate a 2-page investment memo for NVDA\"\n    -> multi-section structured output with exec summary, metrics, risks\n12. Source provenance: every claim must link to exact doc + page + paragraph\n    -> not just 'from 10-K' but 'from 10-K, Risk Factors, para 3, pg 22'\n13. Temporal awareness: \"What changed in guidance since last earnings?\"\n    -> requires version-aware retrieval across time-stamped documents\n14. Sector-wide queries: \"Which semi companies mentioned China risk in latest 10-K?\"\n    -> fan-out across all companies in sector, aggregate results\n15. Confidence + escalation: if confidence <80%, say 'I'm not sure' + escalate\n    -> never present uncertain answers as facts\n\nNFR:\n<5mins latency (interactive), <30min (full report generation)\n200 analysts, ~50% run queries daily = 100 queries/day interactive\n    + 50 scheduled reports/day (batch, off-peak)\n500 symbols coverage, 10 years of filings per symbol\nAccuracy: Very high — analysts verify but don't want noise\nSecurity: Chinese walls — desk A cannot see desk B's annotations/views\nSafety: no investment advice language, no material non-public info leakage\nCost: budget-aware routing (simple→mini, complex→GPT-4o)\nEvaluation metrics:\n    - faithfulness/groundedness per response (automated scoring)\n    - retrieval precision/recall (was the right chunk found?)\n    - budget tracking per user/desk/day\n    - audit log: every LLM call + retrieval + user action logged\n    - rate limiting per user (prevent abuse/cost explosion)\n    - latency p50/p95/p99 tracking\n    - weekly accuracy regression suite (500+ test cases)\n    - human feedback loop: analyst thumbs-up/down → retraining signal",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR:\n1. Freeform Q&A: \"whats current risk, scope, outlook for AAPL\"\n    -> structured, annotated, grounded answer with citations\n2. Company profile subscriptions: user defines watchlist + format\n    -> agent processes async, delivers on schedule (daily/weekly)\n3. Comparative analysis: \"Compare NVDA vs AMD risk factors\" or\n    \"How did AAPL guidance change vs last quarter?\"\n    -> semantic diff across documents, not just retrieval\n4. Multi-hop reasoning: \"Which of my covered companies have supply\n    chain exposure to Taiwan AND revenue >$50B?\"\n    -> decompose into sub-queries (structured filter + semantic + join)\n5. Numerical queries: \"What was NVDA gross margin trend over 4 quarters?\"\n    -> must use structured data/SQL, NOT hallucinate numbers from RAG\n6. Contradiction handling: news says 'beat', analyst says 'miss'\n    -> detect conflicts, present both with source authority ranking\n7. Follow-up / conversational: \"Drill into the top risk\" after prior answer\n    -> maintain context, resolve anaphora (\"the\", \"it\", \"that\")\n8. Chart/table extraction: \"Show me the revenue breakdown table from 10-K pg 47\"\n    -> multi-modal: parse tables, describe charts, extract structured data\n9. Cross-reference resolution: answer mentions 'See Note 12'\n    -> auto-fetch Note 12 content and include in response\n10. Proactive alerts: new 8-K filed for watched company\n    -> detect, summarize, push notification to relevant analyst\n11. Report generation: \"Generate a 2-page investment memo for NVDA\"\n    -> multi-section structured output with exec summary, metrics, risks\n12. Source provenance: every claim must link to exact doc + page + paragraph\n    -> not just 'from 10-K' but 'from 10-K, Risk Factors, para 3, pg 22'\n13. Temporal awareness: \"What changed in guidance since last earnings?\"\n    -> requires version-aware retrieval across time-stamped documents\n14. Sector-wide queries: \"Which semi companies mentioned China risk in latest 10-K?\"\n    -> fan-out across all companies in sector, aggregate results\n15. Confidence + escalation: if confidence <80%, say 'I'm not sure' + escalate\n    -> never present uncertain answers as facts\n\nNFR:\n<5mins latency (interactive), <30min (full report generation)\n200 analysts, ~50% run queries daily = 100 queries/day interactive\n    + 50 scheduled reports/day (batch, off-peak)\n500 symbols coverage, 10 years of filings per symbol\nAccuracy: Very high — analysts verify but don't want noise\nSecurity: Chinese walls — desk A cannot see desk B's annotations/views\nSafety: no investment advice language, no material non-public info leakage\nCost: budget-aware routing (simple→mini, complex→GPT-4o)\nEvaluation metrics:\n    - faithfulness/groundedness per response (automated scoring)\n    - retrieval precision/recall (was the right chunk found?)\n    - budget tracking per user/desk/day\n    - audit log: every LLM call + retrieval + user action logged\n    - rate limiting per user (prevent abuse/cost explosion)\n    - latency p50/p95/p99 tracking\n    - weekly accuracy regression suite (500+ test cases)\n    - human feedback loop: analyst thumbs-up/down → retraining signal",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
